# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets — never commit
.env
*.key

# Runtime output (regenerated each run)
mission-output/
chief-engineer-runs/
sdk/chief-engineer-runs/
sdk/mission-output/
**/.sabotage/

# ParaView crash backtraces from headless start attempts
paraview.*.btr
paraview.*,*.btr

# Mega-batch live/transient files (durable on disk, kept out of git churn)
demo-output/website/mega-batch/work/
demo-output/website/mega-batch/ledger.jsonl
demo-output/website/mega-batch/run.log
demo-output/website/mega-batch/STOP

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- solver run artefacts and live churn (added 2026-07-29) ---
# These are regenerated by every run and must never reach the remote.
# solve_registry alone reached 534 MB of solver logs in one night.
demo-output/website/solve_registry/
demo-output/website/mega-batch/runner.log
demo-output/website/mega-batch/runner.err.log
demo-output/website/mega-batch/runner.pid
demo-output/website/mega-batch/keeper.log
demo-output/website/mega-batch/learned_study.json
demo-output/website/mega-batch/work/
badFaces

# Decomposed parallel state -- rebuilt by decomposePar on demand
**/processor[0-9]*/

# OpenFOAM runtime-compiled code and solver time directories inside scratch runs
**/dynamicCode/
demo-output/website/campaign/D5_rsm_runs/*/[0-9]*/
demo-output/website/campaign/*_runs/*/[0-9]*/

# --- mesh and sampled-field data (added 2026-07-29, after I committed 25M lines) ---
# I ran `git add -A` on a directory that contained solver output and swept in
# polyMesh files of 766,000 lines each. .git reached 513 MB, and this repo is
# pushed to GitHub. A mesh is regenerated by blockMesh/snappyHexMesh from the
# case dictionaries, which ARE tracked -- the mesh itself never needs to be.
**/constant/polyMesh/
**/postProcessing/
*.xy
*.raw
*.obj.gz
*.stl.gz

# Sampled surface/line data written by functionObjects
**/surfaces/
**/sets/

# Laptop bundle build output (the .zip is committed; the extracted tree is not)
dist/certonomous-demo/

# --- F6d random-matrix UQ ensemble (added 2026-07-30) ---
# 84 solver run directories, 2.3 GB of fields and 3 MB logs apiece. Same policy
# as solve_registry above: the runs are on-disk primary evidence at the paths
# cited in campaign/F6d_random_matrix_uq.md, and the scripts that rebuild them
# from the F6b baseline ARE tracked, along with every derived result JSON.
demo-output/website/dafoam/f6d_random_matrix_uq/ens/
demo-output/website/dafoam/f6d_random_matrix_uq/signdemo/
demo-output/website/dafoam/f6d_random_matrix_uq/signcheck/
demo-output/website/dafoam/f6d_random_matrix_uq/f6a_recheck/
# Same rule for the Option A continuation tree (2026-08-11): ~0.5 GB of restarted
# cases, on-disk primary evidence, rebuilt by analyse_option_a.py which IS tracked.
demo-output/website/dafoam/f6d_random_matrix_uq/f6d_option_a/

# LaTeX build artifacts
demo-output/website/latex/*.aux
demo-output/website/latex/*.log
demo-output/website/latex/*.out
demo-output/website/latex/*.toc

# Python wheels are dependencies, not source. Ignored as a CLASS rather than by
# name, so the next wheel dropped at root does not have to be caught by hand.
*.whl

# Retry and batch run products at the repository root. These are run products,
# not source, and the pattern is the class: a rule naming mbc_retry6.log does
# not stop mbc_retry7.log.
/mbc_retry*.err
/mbc_retry*.log
/*_batch.err
/*_batch.log

# NAMED EXCEPTION to the batch rule above, and it is load-bearing. uq_batch.log
# and uq_batch.err are cited as durable evidence by docs/HANDOFF-UQ.md, are
# ruled KEEP, do not sweep in docs/GITIGNORE_PROPOSAL.md, and sit in the
# KEEP_ROOT set of scripts/phase2_move_map.py. docs/HANDSHAKE.md H3a marks them
# DO NOT SWEEP expressly so that a later pass cannot undo the finding. They stay
# tracked. Without these two lines the batch rule would silently pull two
# tracked evidence files into the ignore-matching population.
!/uq_batch.err
!/uq_batch.log

# --- thermal ladder K0: 0.orig/ initial conditions must travel (2026-08-17) ---
# The rule above, `demo-output/website/campaign/*_runs/*/[0-9]*/`, correctly
# excludes solver time directories. `[0-9]*` also matches `0.orig`, which is the
# OpenFOAM convention for the initial conditions a case is REBUILT from and is
# case input, not solver output. A negation on the files alone cannot work --
# git will not descend into an excluded directory -- so the directory is
# re-included first and its contents second.
!demo-output/website/campaign/THERMAL_K0_runs/*/0.orig/
!demo-output/website/campaign/THERMAL_K0_runs/*/0.orig/**

# --- F14 cooling ladder, rungs K0b (mesh sensitivity) and K0c (2026-08-17) ---
# Same policy as the K0 block above and for the same two reasons. Solver time
# directories are run output and are rebuilt from the tracked dictionaries;
# `0.orig/` is case INPUT and must travel, and because `[0-9]*` matches `0.orig`
# the directory is re-included first and its contents second. git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a negation on the files alone does not
# work. The cost of getting this wrong is on record: one `[0-9]*` loop deleted
# every initial-condition directory in the K0b tree.
docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0c_runs/*/[0-9]*/
docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0b_mesh_sensitivity/*/[0-9]*/
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0c_runs/*/0.orig/
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0c_runs/*/0.orig/**
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0b_mesh_sensitivity/*/0.orig/
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0b_mesh_sensitivity/*/0.orig/**

# --- F14 cooling ladder, rung K2b-pilot (2026-08-18) ---
# Same policy, same two reasons, and the same re-inclusion order: `0.orig/` is
# case INPUT and must travel, `0/` and every solved time directory are OUTPUT.
# KV1's run tree tracks its time directories and this one deliberately does not:
# KV1's cases are 1,200 cells, K2b's are 46,400 and 104,400, and eight ascii
# fields per written time at ten time directories per case is the size that put
# .git at 513 MB the last time this was got wrong. Everything a reader needs is
# tracked: the dictionaries, `0.orig/`, the solver logs, COST.txt, CASE.txt,
# SEED.txt and the HEATBALANCE_*.json/.txt audit reports. The run is rebuilt by
# the recipe in `K2b_PILOT_RESULTS.md` section 10.
docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K2b_runs/*/[0-9]*/
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K2b_runs/*/0.orig/
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K2b_runs/*/0.orig/**

# --- BATCH 2: solver output inside the campaign and dafoam run trees (2026-08-17) ---
# `campaign/MOVE_MAP_2026-08-16.md` section 7.2: a run tree's INPUTS stay
# tracked and its OUTPUTS leave tracking. Case dictionaries (`system/`,
# `constant/`) and initial conditions (`0/`, `0.orig/`) are source -- they
# regenerate the run -- while solver time directories and solver logs are
# output, rebuilt by re-running it. Nothing is deleted: every path these rules
# untrack stays on disk at the same path with the same byte count.
#
# SCOPED TO THESE TWO ROOTS ON PURPOSE, and the scope is the ruling. A
# repo-wide `**/log.*` or `**/[0-9]*/` also reaches
# `docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/`, whose run trees R25 sends to
# `verification/runs/` under batch 7. It would not untrack the logs already
# committed there -- a tracked file overrides an ignore rule -- but it WOULD
# silently ignore every solver log the lane writing that tree produces next.
# Those trees are excluded exactly as `MESH_AUDIT_runs` is, and batch 7
# untracks them at their new path. Batch 7 must re-point these two roots when
# it moves them, which is the obligation
# `MOVE_MAP_EXECUTION_2026-08-17.md` section 3.2 already records for lines
# 122-123 above.

# Solver time directories, at any depth under the two roots.
#
# `[1-9]*/` and `0.[0-9]*/` rather than the `[0-9]*/` used above, and the
# difference is 572 files. `[0-9]*/` matches `0/` and `0.orig/` too -- case
# INPUT, 773 and 108 tracked files under these two roots -- so it needs them
# re-included, and a re-inclusion is not free: measured over all 43,663 files
# on disk under these roots, negating `**/0/` and `**/0.orig/` back in stops
# 572 currently-ignored UNTRACKED files from being ignored, because a rule
# above already excluded them at their own depth. Un-ignoring 572 files of
# solver output is how the 25-million-line commit recorded at line 56 happened.
# These two patterns never match `0` or `0.orig` in the first place: `0.orig`
# fails `0.[0-9]` on its `o`, and neither matches a bare `0`. Verified over
# every directory segment on disk under both roots -- 577 distinct
# digit-leading segments, of which exactly three are not purely numeric:
# `0.orig`, `2026-08-08` and `4G_runs`, each handled below or not matched.
demo-output/website/campaign/**/[1-9]*/
demo-output/website/campaign/**/0.[0-9]*/
demo-output/website/dafoam/**/[1-9]*/
demo-output/website/dafoam/**/0.[0-9]*/

# `4G_runs` is a run TREE whose name begins with a digit, 42 tracked files, and
# `[1-9]*/` would otherwise ignore the whole of it. git will not descend into an
# excluded directory, so the directory itself is re-included; the time
# directories inside it are still matched by the rules above, which come first
# and are not negated for anything below `4G_runs`.
!demo-output/website/campaign/4G_runs/

# Solver logs under the two roots.
demo-output/website/campaign/**/log.*
demo-output/website/campaign/**/*.log
demo-output/website/campaign/**/*.log.*
demo-output/website/dafoam/**/log.*
demo-output/website/dafoam/**/*.log
demo-output/website/dafoam/**/*.log.*

# NAMED EXCEPTION, and it is the ruling of 2026-08-17 written where a reader of
# the rule will meet it. `MESH_AUDIT_runs` holds 78 tracked files and every one
# is a `*.log.checkMesh` under a dated directory, so the rules above reach the
# whole tree and batch 2 would take its last tracked file -- after which batch
# 7's `git mv` of it aborts, taking every other source in that invocation with
# it. Option A was ruled: batch 2 spares it, and it is untracked at
# `verification/runs/MESH_AUDIT_runs` once batch 7 has moved it. The negation
# lives here so the sparing is legible from the rule and not only from a
# record, and it re-includes nothing that was ignored before it: 78 files on
# disk, 78 tracked, 0 ignored. REMOVING IT IS PART OF BATCH 7.
!demo-output/website/campaign/MESH_AUDIT_runs/
!demo-output/website/campaign/MESH_AUDIT_runs/**

# --- F14 cooling ladder, rung K0c-T (turbulent, 2026-08-18) ---
# Same policy as K0c above: time directories and meshes are rebuilt from the
# committed dictionaries, and `0.orig/` is the initial-condition directory the
# case is REBUILT FROM and is kept.  `build_cases.py` was verified from a fresh
# temporary directory to regenerate all nine cases' dictionaries byte-identically.
#
# AND ONE THING THIS RUNG HAD TO DROP, RECORDED RATHER THAN LEFT SILENT: its nine
# solver logs total 511 MB, because one case ran 140 000 outer iterations to
# establish that it never reaches steady state.  Gzipped they are still ~90 MB.
# They are ignored, and replaced by two GENERATED, COMMITTED artefacts per case:
#   * `LOG_DIGEST.txt` -- the whole header verbatim (every control's in-log
#     witness of its plant), the solve counts the controls are graded on, a
#     decimated body, the last 120 lines, and the SHA-256 of the log it came from;
#   * `MONITOR.tsv` -- the in-pass series the convergence verdict is actually
#     taken on, which the blanket `**/postProcessing/` rule above would otherwise
#     hide, as it hides the laminar rung's.
# What is lost is the per-iteration residual trace between samples.
docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0cT_runs/*/[0-9]*/
docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0cT_runs/*/constant/polyMesh/
docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0cT_runs/*/log.buoyantBoussinesqSimpleFoam*
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0cT_runs/*/0.orig/
!docs/campaigns/F14-cooling-ladder/K0cT_runs/*/0.orig/**
